From: hawkff <109485367+hawkff@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 19:55:39 +0000
Subject: Match the start screen to the browser theme

Since Android 12 the system shows a start screen whenever the browser
starts without a running activity. It is drawn from the theme in the
manifest, so it follows the system's dark mode, not the browser's own
theme setting, and it does not follow the browser's AMOLED black
setting.

On Android 13 and later, set the theme of the next start screen from the
browser's theme setting: light for Light, dark gray for Dark, black for
Dark with AMOLED black, and light by day and black at night for System
default with AMOLED black. System default without AMOLED black resets to
the theme in the manifest. The themes show no icon, like the tabbed
browser theme.

Android looks the theme up by name, so the names are kept in release
builds. The theme is set right after the theme setting or the AMOLED
black switch is written, and once per process in deferred startup, after
the first frame. Within a process it is set again only when it changes.
Android keeps one start screen theme per app, so custom tabs and web
apps started from the home screen use it too. Android 12 has no such
setting and is unchanged.

